completed_at: "2026-11-20T12:31:03.341Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: The spec compares every parameter-derived context_intent field of the flat and nested reads and only requires estimated_tokens to be a number on both; it passes regardless of which concurrent read waits on the context-usage ledger
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: low
resolution: "tests/unit/mcp/read-tool-flat-parameters.spec.ts compares every context_intent field except estimated_tokens, which measures the rendered output and depends on context-usage ledger state that both concurrent reads write, and requires that estimate to be a number on both sides"
expected_result: Flat and nested MCP read arguments are proven to resolve the same intent regardless of concurrent ledger timing
actual_result: The spec passes locally and in the full coverage run; the comparison no longer depends on which concurrent read waits on the ledger
